        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing, and one answer has to be chosen. Choose the answer the documents support better.\n\nQuestion: What political party was James Humphrey affiliated with?\n\nAnswer A: Republican\n  about: James Humphrey\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"He was elected as a Republican to the Thirty-sixth Congress (March 4, 1859 – March 3, 1861).\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Democratic\n  about: James Humphrey\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"During this period he was instrumental in merging the state ’s Democratic and Farmer-Labor parties.\" [document 2]\n\nThe documents:\nDocument 1: James Humphrey (New York politician) James Humphrey (October 9, 1811 – June 16, 1866) was a U.S. Representative from New York. Born in Fairfield, Connecticut, Humphrey pursued classical studies under his father Heman Humphrey. He was graduated from Amherst College in 1831. He studied law. He was admitted to the bar and practiced. He moved to Louisville, Kentucky, in 1837 and one year later to Brooklyn, New York. Humphrey was elected as a Republican to the Thirty-sixth Congress (March 4, 1859 – March 3, 1861). He was an unsuccessful candidate for reelection in 1860 to the Thirty-seventh Congress and for\nDocument 2: University of Minnesota , where he received his bachelor ’ s degree in 1939 . He did graduate work at Louisiana State University and returned to Minnesota to teach college and work as a radio commentator in the Twin Cities . In 1944 he became the Minnesota campaign manager for U.S. Pres . Franklin D. Roosevelt . During this period he was instrumental in merging the state ’ s Democratic and Farmer-Labor parties . After an unsuccessful bid for mayor of Minneapolis in 1943 , Humphrey won election two years later . At the Democratic National Convention in 1948 ,\n\nWeigh the evidence. Which documents are specific, and consistent within themselves: do their names, dates and other details fit together? Which fit what the other documents say? Does any document read as altered, or out of place? Judge by the documents alone.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"reason\": \"one or two sentences\", \"choice\": \"A\"}"
